@ [canonical_uuid] f1fd1689-f290-4be6-ad82-e36d58103e1b
@ [typed_p03_commit] af3f8137ca695d5a3eb49c3a8a2ede7dcafd4cf6

& [Inspected]
  + crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/staged_diff_acquisition.rs GitRunner acquisition identity snapshot bounded drains canonical path and bounded file hashing
  + crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/sjs_commit_placement_acquisition.rs parallel GitRunner and bounded output implementation
  + crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/self_work_update_broker_b1_cdrive_windows_containment.rs suspended-process job assignment kill-on-close bounded drains timeout and forced termination pattern

& [ReusablePatterns]
  + preincrement and cap command count before launch
  + absolute executable and repository working directory cleared environment C locale null stdin concurrent bounded stdout and stderr drains stderr refusal and unsuccessful-exit refusal
  + disable system and global config terminal prompts optional locks lazy fetch replace objects system attributes and file protocol
  + sample repository root branch HEAD object format Git directory index executable and index before and after then refuse any drift
  + bounded raw file hashing and explicit checked byte accounting
  + on Windows create suspended assign to kill-on-close job before resume then enforce deadline and terminate the job on timeout or output overflow

& [MustNotReuse]
  + staged diff cached index inventory rename detection record parsing and blob semantics do not enter RSO
  + the existing GitRunner accepts arbitrary string slices and lacks the signed per-command allowlist required by RSO-012
  + the existing staged and placement run_bounded_command functions wait without a timeout and therefore do not satisfy RSO-020
  + fs canonicalize followed by fs metadata follows links and does not independently prove the RSO-007 RSO-008 no-follow boundary
  + the B1 Windows containment primitive requires a different crate-private authority permit and cannot be called or treated as RSO authority

& [P04Decisions]
  + define a private closed GitOperation enum whose variants alone emit version build-options identity ls-tree commit and blob commands
  + pass every supplied locator only after the exact ls-tree double-dash boundary and never expose an arbitrary argument runner
  + add component-wise link or Windows reparse-point refusal before canonical equality checks for executable repository Git directory index and requested paths
  + implement an RSO-owned bounded deadline runner with process-tree containment whose authorization originates only after SjsRsoRequest validation
  + preserve env_clear and add explicit no-credential no-prompt values while retaining an absolute executable so no PATH is needed
  + keep current Cantor observation impossible in fixture tests by requiring a distinct disposable fixture input class and root

& [OpenImplementationChecks]
  + prove exact Windows reparse-point refusal API and Unix component symlink refusal with platform-focused unit tests
  + prove timeout kills the complete spawned Git process tree without borrowing B1 permission identity
  + prove exact command vectors independently before the first disposable fixture launch

& [Effects]
  + read-only source inspection only with zero Git invocation repository observation process start filesystem mutation provider model network remote or external effect
